1. PURPOSE

The Exergic Commons License ("ECL") grants broad permission to exercise copyright and other software rights controlled by a Licensor while withholding that permission where the exercise of those rights materially enables specified forms of coercive capture, systemic domination, deceptive manipulation, repressive surveillance, unlawful political repression, or comparable reductions of meaningful human agency.

The ethical principles motivating this License are described in `spec/PRINCIPLES.md`. Those principles aid interpretation but do not independently create restrictions beyond the operative terms of this License, the exact Restricted Parties Schedule incorporated by the applicable Software release, and applicable law.

This License is intended to operate through rights that a Licensor actually owns or is authorized to license. It does not create a copyright prohibition over an act merely by calling that act a Prohibited Use.

2. DEFINITIONS

"Software" means the source code, object code, documentation, and other copyrightable material to which a copyright holder or other authorized rightsholder has applied this License.

"Licensor" means a copyright holder or other person or entity authorized to grant one or more Licensed Rights in the Software. Each Licensor acts only with respect to rights that Licensor owns or is authorized to license.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising Licensed Rights under this License.

"Licensed Rights" means only those copyright, software-exploitation, and equivalent rights in the Software that a particular Licensor owns or is authorized to license and for which applicable law requires that Licensor's permission. Depending on the applicable law and facts, Licensed Rights may include reproduction; translation, adaptation, arrangement, modification, or creation of derivative works; distribution; and loading, displaying, running, transmission, or storage to the extent those acts require an authorization controlled by the Licensor. Licensed Rights do not include patent or trademark rights and do not include an act to the extent applicable law permits that act without the Licensor's authorization notwithstanding this License.

"Control" means the direct or indirect power to direct the management or policies of an entity, whether through ownership of voting interests, contract, appointment rights, or comparable means.

"Restricted Party" means a person, legal entity, governmental body, agency, military body, or other organization expressly designated in the exact Restricted Parties Schedule incorporated by the applicable Software release.

"Covered Associate" means, solely in relation to a particular use or project, a person or entity that You know or reasonably should know is materially acting for, under the direction or Control of, on behalf of, or for the material benefit of a Restricted Party. Covered Associate includes a contractor, consultant, controlled affiliate, material project collaborator, intermediary, or service provider when the relevant activity materially supports a Restricted Party. Mere historical contact, incidental interaction, ordinary consumer use, or remote social association does not by itself create Covered Associate status.

"Material Participation" means participation that makes a non-trivial contribution to the design, financing, governance, development, training, operation, deployment, commercialization, targeting, decision-making, or material outputs of a project.

"Restricted Project" means a project, program, deployment, contract, research effort, service, product, or coordinated activity that either:

(a) is expressly designated as a Restricted Project in the exact Restricted Parties Schedule incorporated by the applicable Software release;
(b) has Material Participation by a Restricted Party;
(c) has Material Participation by a Covered Associate in connection with the Restricted Party;
(d) is performed at the direction of, on behalf of, or primarily for the material benefit of a Restricted Party; or
(e) is structured through an intermediary, contractor, consortium, affiliate, or other arrangement with the purpose or substantial effect of avoiding a restriction in this License.

A project does not become a Restricted Project solely because an unrelated participant has an incidental or unknown connection to a Restricted Party.

"Restricted Parties Schedule" or "Schedule" means the exact immutable versioned document incorporated by the applicable Software release that lists Restricted Parties, Restricted Projects, and any expressly defined class-based designations or exclusions. The Schedule must be objectively identifiable by an immutable version, content hash, or exact ECL Bundle manifest. A mutable branch, `latest` page, registry view, or channel pointer is not by itself an incorporated Schedule. A later Schedule never retroactively alters the Licensed Rights or restrictions attached to an earlier Software release; adopting a different Schedule requires a new exact ECL Bundle for a new Software release.

"ECL Bundle" or "Bundle" means the exact combination of the ECL License version and exact Restricted Parties Schedule incorporated by a Software release, identified by an immutable manifest or equivalent release metadata that pins the relevant artifacts and their cryptographic hashes.

"Prohibited Use" means a use context described in Section 5 in which Licensed Rights may not be exercised as provided by that Section.

"Independent Remediation Activity" means an activity whose principal and actual purpose is to investigate, document, challenge, audit, review, prosecute, defend against, remedy, disclose, or prevent a Prohibited Use or the conduct forming the basis of a Restricted Party or Restricted Project designation, provided that the relevant person or function:

(a) is operationally independent from the persons or functions directing or materially participating in the underlying prohibited conduct;
(b) does not itself materially participate in that conduct except in an investigative, judicial, defence, audit, oversight, disclosure, or remedial capacity;
(c) does not exercise Licensed Rights to continue, conceal, optimize, or materially support the underlying Prohibited Use or Restricted Project; and
(d) limits exercise of Licensed Rights to what is reasonably necessary for the remedial purpose.

3. GRANT OF LICENSED RIGHTS

Subject to the conditions and restrictions of this License, each Licensor grants You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to exercise all Licensed Rights that the particular Licensor owns or is authorized to license in the Software.

Accordingly, to the extent a relevant act requires a Licensed Right, this grant permits You to reproduce, load, run, inspect, study, modify, adapt, translate, combine, create derivative works from, distribute, deploy, and provide services using the Software, subject to this License.

You may exercise Licensed Rights for personal, academic, scientific, educational, governmental, non-profit, or commercial purposes except where that exercise is prohibited by Sections 5 or 6 or forms part of a Restricted Project.

Sections 4, 5, and 6 are conditions on the Licensed Rights granted by this Section. If an activity does not exercise a Licensed Right and does not otherwise require a Licensor's authorization under applicable law, this License does not transform that activity into copyright infringement merely because the activity falls within a factual description used by this License.

This License does not assume that an independent contract has been formed for conduct outside the Licensed Rights. Section 6 describes a separate Hosted-Service Covenant for the narrow service-provider gap identified there, but that covenant exists only where applicable law finds independently sufficient formation, assent, authority, consideration or other required legal basis, and enforceability. No contractual obligation or remedy beyond the Licensed Rights arises merely because this License labels conduct restricted.

4. DISTRIBUTION AND BUNDLE-PRESERVATION CONDITIONS

If You distribute the Software or a substantial portion of it, modified or unmodified, in exercise of Licensed Rights, You must:

(a) preserve copyright, attribution, and license notices;
(b) provide a copy of this License or an unambiguous immutable reference to the exact ECL License version governing the distributed Software;
(c) provide the exact Schedule governing the distributed Software in a form that accompanies the distributed copy and allows the recipient to read the operative Restricted Party, Restricted Project, class-designation, and exclusion entries without consulting mutable project state;
(d) preserve and provide immutable Bundle metadata identifying the exact License and exact Schedule, including their immutable versions or identifiers and cryptographic hashes, so the recipient can verify which artifacts govern the distributed copy without consulting a mutable `latest`, branch, registry view, or channel;
(e) identify material modifications made by You; and
(f) not represent the Software as OSI-approved open source unless a future version has separately received such approval.

A Bundle manifest, hash, repository-relative path, or other identifier may verify the Schedule supplied under paragraph (c), but does not by itself substitute for providing the operative Schedule. A distributor may instead provide a demonstrably retrievable immutable content-addressed copy only where the reference itself remains sufficient for the recipient to retrieve and read the exact Schedule independently of any mutable branch, channel, registry view, repository-relative path, or later project state.

For an original application of ECL by a Licensor to material over which that Licensor controls the relevant Licensed Rights, if that Licensor's own initial release materials fail to identify an exact incorporated Schedule objectively, the Schedule for **that Licensor's grant in that material and that release only** is deemed empty. That limited fallback does not remove the independent Section 5 conditions.

The empty-Schedule fallback cannot erase, replace, weaken, or re-resolve an exact upstream Bundle already governing ECL-covered material received from another Licensor. A downstream distributor or modifier must preserve each applicable upstream Schedule and Bundle under paragraphs (c) and (d). Failure to do so is a breach of this Section; it does not make an upstream Schedule empty, does not substitute a later or mutable Schedule, and does not expand any downstream recipient's rights in the upstream material.

You may license Your own original additions under additional terms, provided those terms do not purport to remove or weaken restrictions that continue to apply to ECL-covered material or grant rights in another Licensor's material that You do not possess.

Each downstream recipient who receives ECL-covered material may independently exercise Licensed Rights granted directly by each relevant Licensor under the ECL terms applicable to that recipient's exact copy or release, provided the recipient independently complies with those terms. A downstream distributor's omission or corruption of required Schedule or Bundle information does not grant the recipient broader rights than the relevant upstream Licensor granted.

5. PROHIBITED USE CONTEXTS — CONDITIONS ON LICENSED RIGHTS

As a condition of the grant in Section 3, You may not knowingly exercise any Licensed Right in or to the Software where that exercise materially enables or supports any of the following. References in this Section to using, deploying, training, integrating, hosting, or otherwise employing the Software describe the factual context of the conditioned exercise of Licensed Rights; they do not assert a freestanding copyright right over conduct that applicable law does not reserve to a Licensor.

5.1 Repressive surveillance.
Systematic surveillance, tracking, identification, or profiling of persons or populations for the purpose of political repression, persecution, unlawful intimidation, arbitrary detention, or suppression of lawful dissent.

5.2 Coercive targeting.
Selection, prioritization, scoring, targeting, or operational support intended to facilitate unlawful violence, torture, enforced disappearance, collective punishment, or intentional attacks against civilians or other persons protected by applicable international law.

5.3 Systematic discriminatory domination.
Automated or data-driven systems whose primary purpose is to impose unlawful discrimination or systematically deny fundamental rights on the basis of protected personal characteristics.

5.4 Deceptive population manipulation.
Large-scale systems primarily designed to deliberately deceive a population about material facts in order to remove meaningful political, civic, or personal agency, excluding ordinary persuasion, advertising, satire, fiction, or clearly disclosed simulation.

5.5 Irreversible coercive capture.
Systems primarily designed to create or maintain coercive technological dependence, informational control, or decision-making asymmetry where affected persons or communities are intentionally denied a meaningful ability to understand, contest, exit, or seek an alternative, and where that denial materially restricts fundamental rights or civic autonomy.

5.6 Systematic coercive domination and unlawful political repression.
Systems, deployments, operational processes, or material Software-enabled capabilities whose primary purpose, or whose known and reasonably foreseeable material function in the relevant deployment, is to enable or maintain systematic persecution, unlawful political repression, torture or comparably severe cruel, inhuman, or degrading treatment, enforced disappearance, arbitrary detention, collective punishment, forced labour, forced displacement or expulsion without meaningful individualized protection, severe discriminatory domination, or a comparable coercive denial of fundamental rights or of the practical ability to dissent, contest, or exit.

Ordinary lawful criminal justice, immigration administration, military service, employment, public-health action, emergency response, content moderation, public administration, or other compulsory activity is not prohibited merely because it is coercive, restrictive, controversial, or governmental. Capital punishment, detention, deportation, conscription, protest regulation, and similar exercises of State power are not standalone ECL categories; the relevant Software-enabled context must independently satisfy the elements of this or another subsection.

5.7 Circumvention.
Exercise of Licensed Rights through an arrangement whose principal purpose is to enable conduct that another provision of this License expressly prohibits.

A context is not prohibited merely because it is controversial, politically disputed, military-adjacent, commercial, governmental, security-related, or capable of dual use. The relevant exercise of Licensed Rights must satisfy the substantive criteria above or fall within a Restricted Project.

6. RESTRICTED PARTIES, PROJECTS, AND SERVICE PROVISION

No Licensed Rights are granted under this License to a Restricted Party for the applicable Software release except to the limited extent expressly permitted by the Independent Remediation Activity provision below. This withholding applies only to rights a Licensor is legally entitled to withhold and does not purport to negate statutory rights, exhausted rights, or other permissions that applicable law makes available independently of this License.

You may not knowingly exercise Licensed Rights as part of a Restricted Project.

You may not knowingly exercise any Licensed Right to reproduce, adapt, modify, configure where configuration constitutes adaptation, distribute, install, deploy where deployment requires reproduction, update, scale where scaling requires reproduction, transmit where transmission implicates a Licensed Right, or otherwise provision or maintain the Software for the purpose of providing a Restricted Party or Restricted Project with the Software, a derivative work, hosted functionality, integration, model, dataset transformation, technical service, or other material Software-enabled capability where You know or reasonably should know that the exercise of that Licensed Right materially enables or supports the Restricted Party or Restricted Project.

For avoidance of doubt, where You operate the Software to provide remote or hosted functionality, this Section first conditions the provider's **actual exercise of Licensed Rights** in establishing, provisioning, modifying, updating, scaling, or maintaining the service. A remote user who merely receives functionality or output and does not itself exercise a Licensed Right is not deemed a copyright licensee solely because it used the remote service.

A provider may have lawfully established a long-lived or multi-tenant deployment before it knows that a later customer is a Restricted Party or that a later use is part of a Restricted Project. If, after that knowledge arises, continued service from the already established deployment can occur without any further exercise of a Licensed Right, this License does **not** deem the later service request itself an exercise of copyright or another Licensed Right merely to manufacture an infringement theory.

To address that service-provider gap without inventing a copyright-exclusive right, the following **Hosted-Service Covenant** applies only where an independently enforceable contract incorporating this License is formed under applicable law. Where You, with legally sufficient notice of these terms, assent to such a contract or applicable law otherwise treats Your knowing acceptance or exercise of ECL-granted rights as sufficient assent, You covenant that after You know or reasonably should know that a customer, beneficiary, project, or materially supported activity is a Restricted Party or Restricted Project under the exact Bundle governing Your Software copy or release, You will not knowingly continue to provide that party or project with material Software-enabled hosted functionality or capability except to the extent permitted as an Independent Remediation Activity.

The Hosted-Service Covenant is deliberately contractual. Its breach does not by itself constitute copyright infringement where the complained-of conduct does not exercise a Licensed Right. Contractual obligations and remedies exist only to the extent the relevant jurisdiction recognizes the required formation, assent, authority, consideration or other legal basis, enforceability, and remedy. If no such contract exists, ECL reaches the provider only when and to the extent the provider actually exercises a Licensed Right or another authorization controlled by the relevant Licensor.

A person who is a Covered Associate only because of a professional or project-specific relationship is not permanently restricted from unrelated personal or professional activity after that relationship ceases, unless that person is separately designated as a Restricted Party in the applicable Schedule.

Notwithstanding the preceding restrictions, a person or function otherwise within the scope of a Restricted Party may exercise Licensed Rights solely to conduct an Independent Remediation Activity. This exception may apply, where its definition is actually satisfied, to an independent court or tribunal, ombuds or National Preventive Mechanism function, inspector, auditor, prosecutor investigating official abuse, independent legal defence function, public-interest accountability body, or comparable remedial function.

A person relying on this exception must have reasonably documented grounds for concluding that the Independent Remediation Activity definition is satisfied. The exception does not authorize ordinary operational, intelligence, military, policing, detention, immigration, procurement, surveillance, targeting, administrative, or commercial activity merely because it is described as compliance, oversight, safety, accountability, or remediation.

7. KNOWLEDGE STANDARD

Except for a person or entity expressly designated as a Restricted Party, or a project expressly designated as a Restricted Project, restrictions based on association, participation, benefit, or project status apply where You actually know, or where a reasonable person in Your position would have substantial grounds to know, the facts creating the restriction.

You are not required to conduct unlimited investigations into remote ownership chains, unknown collaborators, passive investors, or undisclosed relationships. Deliberate avoidance of readily available facts does not defeat this Section.

8. GOVERNANCE AND DESIGNATIONS

The repository maintaining ECL should publish a governance procedure describing how Restricted Parties and Restricted Projects are proposed, evaluated, challenged, reviewed, added, narrowed, or removed.

A Schedule designation should be based on documented evidence and a reasoned conclusion that the designated party or project materially and systematically participates in, directs, enables, or derives substantial benefit from conduct substantially matching one or more Section 5 criteria, or deliberately circumvents an ECL restriction. Mere political disagreement, nationality, ethnicity, religion, ideology, military status, commercial size, or remote association is insufficient.

A designation should identify the narrowest reasonably knowable actor, project, apparatus, or determinable class supported by the evidence and should state material exclusions or remedial functions where necessary to avoid overbreadth.

For license-compliance purposes, however, an express designation or exclusion in the exact Schedule incorporated by the applicable Software release controls. A licensee is not required to independently re-litigate the evidentiary basis for every Schedule entry in order to determine whether the entry applies.

The governance procedure and supporting evidence do not themselves modify the operative license attached to a Software release. A designation becomes binding for a particular Software release only through the exact Schedule expressly incorporated by that release.

9. NON-RETROACTIVITY AND IMMUTABLE RELEASE STATE

Once a Licensor releases a particular version of the Software under a specific ECL Bundle, later amendments to ECL, the Schedule, governance records, evidence, registry views, channels, or classifications do not retroactively alter the Licensed Rights or restrictions attached to that released Bundle.

A new Software release may adopt a later ECL License version or Schedule by creating or resolving a new exact Bundle.

Moving a mutable channel such as `stable`, `stable-1`, `candidate`, or `draft` does not change the Bundle already attached to an earlier Software release.

10. TERMINATION, AUTHORITY, AND REINSTATEMENT

Rights granted by a particular Licensor under this License terminate only with respect to the Licensed Rights that particular Licensor granted, and only as provided by this Section. Notice may be given by that Licensor or by a person or entity the Licensor has authorized to administer or enforce the relevant grant. One Licensor does not, merely by being a Licensor, have authority to terminate rights granted by another Licensor.

A notice intended to trigger termination under this Section must identify with reasonable specificity: (a) the affected Licensor or Licensors whose grant is asserted to be terminable; (b) the ECL-covered material, contribution, or other objectively identifiable portion of Software to which that grant relates; (c) the affected Software release and exact ECL Bundle, where objectively identifiable from the relevant release materials; (d) the Licensed Rights or grant whose termination is asserted; (e) the material breach and the facts reasonably sufficient to understand it; (f) the authority of the notifying party to act for each affected Licensor; and (g) any applicable cure deadline. A notice does not terminate rights beyond the affected grant, material, release, Bundle, and Licensor scope that it objectively identifies.

For a knowing violation of Sections 5 or 6, the affected Licensor's identified grant terminates with respect to the identified affected Software if You fail to cease and cure the violation within thirty (30) days after receiving a notice satisfying the preceding paragraph. For deliberate circumvention under Section 5.7, termination of the identified affected grant may take effect upon such notice without a cure period.

For any other material breach of a condition of the Licensed Rights, the affected Licensor's identified grant terminates if You fail to cure the breach within thirty (30) days after receiving a notice satisfying the notice requirements above.

Termination is limited to rights actually granted by the affected Licensor and objectively identified by the terminating notice. It does not itself transfer, extinguish, or terminate rights owned or independently granted by another rightsholder, another Bundle, another Software release, or material outside the identified affected grant.

A downstream recipient who obtained an ECL-covered copy before Your termination and who holds an independent direct grant from the relevant Licensor remains governed by that recipient's own compliance and is not automatically terminated solely because Your grant terminated.

After termination, rights from the affected Licensor are reinstated only if that Licensor or an authorized enforcement agent expressly reinstates them, unless applicable law requires a different result. A reinstatement may be unconditional or subject to lawful written conditions. Cure before the applicable termination deadline prevents termination under the relevant notice.

A breach of the Hosted-Service Covenant described in Section 6 is governed by independently applicable contract law and remedies where that covenant forms part of an enforceable contract. It does not automatically terminate a copyright or other Licensed Right grant under this Section unless the independently applicable contract and law validly provide for that result, or the provider separately commits a breach involving an exercise of Licensed Rights that satisfies the termination rules above.

11. STATUTORY RIGHTS, EXCEPTIONS, EXHAUSTION, AND MANDATORY LAW

Nothing in this License restricts an act to the extent applicable law permits that act without authorization from the relevant Licensor notwithstanding the terms of this License, or makes the relevant statutory right, exception, limitation, or privilege non-waivable.

An act performed solely under such an independent statutory permission is not an exercise of Licensed Rights granted by this License merely because the Software is involved.

Nothing in this License is intended to recreate a copyright distribution right that applicable law has exhausted with respect to a particular copy. Exhaustion of a distribution right does not by itself grant permission to reproduce, adapt, modify, or otherwise exercise a distinct Licensed Right that remains controlled by a Licensor.

Nothing in this Section determines whether a waivable statutory default may be altered by a separately valid contract. ECL does not rely on an assumed contract outside the Licensed Rights except for the Hosted-Service Covenant described in Section 6, and that covenant applies only where an independently enforceable contract incorporating it is formed under applicable law.

